    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"It is a chance to live a normal life,\" said 28-year-old Rabia, a recent participant of the Aga Khan University Hospital's new kidney transplant programme speaking at an awareness session for people with chronic kidney disease. \"My options were limited to dialysis, as long as it was possible, or a kidney transplant. This is a new lease on life.\"",
